> Robert Barber wrote:

> Named weapons (not other objects) should carry across bonesfiles.

I actually have a fairly substantial YANI along these lines I've been
thinking about lately, sort of a legacy artifact system.  Naming your
weapon (to something other than the traditional artifacts, of course),
then dying, would have a slim chance (greater as the player gains
levels, but never occuring unless the player has reached Expert in the
weapon) of creating an artifact weapon by that name.  (If the weapon
were not named there would be a somewhat lesser chance, with the
artifact getting name something like "The (weapon) of (dead player's
name)".)

These artifacts wouldn't exist in the spoilers, so the player would
have to discover their abilities through experimentation.  Their
abilities would be drawn from a subset of the abilities the player had
when he died.  They wouldn't be as powerful as the "stock" artifacts,
but would be a nice middle-ground between the "plain ol" weapons and
the likes of Excalibur, while still being potentially more useful than
things like Giantslayer.

